surface-prestrain-extension.out
Prestrained triangle: the row of f0 along the element normal does not change the results
StaticStructural nsteps 2 deltat 1.0 rtolv 1.e-11 maxiter 20 manrmsteps 1 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 3d
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 9 nelem 3 ncrosssect 1 nmat 1 nbc 9 nic 0 nltf 2 nset 3
# Three identical triangles (nodes 1-3, 4-6, 7-9) of surface-prestrain-normal.in. Triangle 1 has its surface
# prestrain f0, which maps the original configuration onto the element plane (no row along the element normal
# n). Triangles 2 and 3 have f0 + c n (x) N with c = 1.3 and -0.8, N the normal of the original configuration
# that the element computes from f0, i.e. a full 3D prestrain that also stretches the normal. In the element
# frame this fills only the third row with c N, which F e3 = 0 removes from F f0, so all three triangles have the
# reactions of surface-prestrain-normal.in and the same global F (IST 156).
node 1 coords 3 -0.326099033699941 0.1130495168499705 0.5
